{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1543958304,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIwMDU0OTk0Njc="},"added":["metadata"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1544022557,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NDUxNjczNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-444516736"},"message":"Here is a reproducible demo to develop a test:\n\n```\ndatalad rev-create 3055\ndatalad install -d . -s https://github.com/datalad/testrepo--minimalds.git sub\ndatalad aggregate-metadata --update-mode target -r\n# fails to access\ndatalad metadata --reporton datasets sub\n```","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1544022557,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE1ODk1NTMzMQ=="},"target":"e4fd9bd38aa7c9458258bb79a57067bccf89d2b84adb64fa3620ac1fee313470","message":"Here is a reproducible demo to develop a test:\n\n```\ndatalad rev-create 3055\ndatalad install -d . -s https://github.com/datalad/testrepo--minimalds.git sub\ndatalad aggregate-metadata --update-mode target -r\n# fails to access\ndatalad metadata --reporton datasets sub\n# remove subds in question\ndatalad uninstall sub\n# works now\ndatalad metadata --reporton datasets sub\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1544026087,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NDU0MTE0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-444541143"},"message":"The core issue is found here: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/master/datalad/metadata/metadata.py#L953-L978\n\nA superdataset will not be queried for metadata of a subdataset or its content when the subdataset is present.\n\nBut I think it is actually worse, as the flow in the query procedure has a somewhat limited ability to deal with this.\n1. Paths are sorted under locally present datasets\n2. For each discovered dataset the closest dataset (upwards) is asked for metadata, if that doesn't have it, the query fails\n\nDatasets are processed in the order in which path annotation finds them, which limits possibilties to change this behavior (if this should be kept -- it was a requested thing at some point).\n\nPossible fixes:\n- query and report for the deepest subdatasets first, and dynamically re-sort failed paths into a more super dataset for re-query -- seems messy\n- always and only report from the metadata that is actually present in the queried (`--dataset`) dataset\n- RF path sorting to amend it with resorting of paths assigned to datasets that have no metadata present (at all), and afterwards continue as-is\n\nThe second and third approach have their benefits, but likely the third is the viable path forward, as it avoid required aggregation into superdatasets for querying hierarchies of datasets. However, it is more messy then the second approach, as only this one is guaranteed to give identical results regardless of subdataset presence.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1544033247,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NDU4NDQ5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-444584492"},"message":"I could be totally wrong (my understanding of the flow/logic in this code is not yet superb), but couldn't it be just a matter of extending the check [here](https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/master/datalad/metadata/metadata.py#L939) with either that dataset contains **any** aggregated metadata (i.e. smth like\n```python\nif op.lexists(op.join(ap['path], agginfo_relpath)):\n    to_query = ap['path']\nelse:\n    lgr.info(\"Dataset %(path)s is installed, but lacks aggregated metadata. Querying superdataset\", ap)\n    to_query = ap['parentds']\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1544033456,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NDU4NTY2NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-444585664"},"message":"More complete:\n```python\n            if ap.get('state', None) == 'absent' or \\\n                    ap.get('type', 'dataset') != 'dataset':\n                # this is a lonely absent dataset/file or content in a present dataset\n                # -\u003e query through parent\n                # there must be a parent, otherwise this would be a non-dataset path\n                # and would have errored during annotation\n                to_query = ap['parentds']\n            else:\n                to_query = ap['path']\n```\nto\n```python\n            if ap.get('state', None) == 'absent' or \\\n                    ap.get('type', 'dataset') != 'dataset':\n                # this is a lonely absent dataset/file or content in a present dataset\n                # -\u003e query through parent\n                # there must be a parent, otherwise this would be a non-dataset path\n                # and would have errored during annotation\n                lgr.info(\"Dataset %(path)s is not installed. Querying superdataset\", ap)\n                to_query = ap['parentds']\n            elif ap.get('type', 'dataset') == 'dataset' and not op.lexists(op.join(ap['path], agginfo_relpath)):\n               lgr.info(\"Dataset %(path)s is installed, but lacks aggregated metadata. Querying superdataset\", ap)\n               to_query = ap['parentds']\n            else:\n                to_query = ap['path']\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1544075988,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NDc1ODA1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-444758059"},"message":"This would fix the immediate issue demo'ed above, but there is no guarantee that the 'parentds' has the metadata and not the parent of the parent or even further away.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1552960559,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3NDE2NzQ1NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-474167454"},"message":"I was digging into this, although probably useless in light of https://github.com/datalad/datalad-revolution/pull/84 , I just hoped that there would be a quick fix for me...  The major blow (and possibly a \"hint on workaround\") is actually the difference between calls `metadata subds` and `metadata -d . subds`.  In the realm of discussion #3230 - in the former (no `-d`) case the \"context\" of path  annotation completely switches over into `subds`, so there is no information about `parentds` in `ap` record, and thus it is not possible to query it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1554705186,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4MDcwMTcxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-480701711"},"message":"FTR: After some thinking in https://github.com/datalad/datalad-revolution/pull/84 I conclude that there is no single \"best\" way to decide which metadata to report without knowledge about the context of such a query. Consequently, `metadata()` is abandoned and replaced by two dedicated commands:\n\n1. `extract_metadata()` - reports metadata from dataset content by running extractors. Metadata is not placed into a dataset, and no potentially existing aggregated metadata is investigated.\n2. `query_metadata()` - reports based on aggregated metadata from a given (or current) dataset. No extractors are invoked, no searching for \"better\" metadata in any subdataset is performed.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1554727761,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4MDgxNzc4OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-480817788"},"message":"Why plain `metadata` couldn't just correspond to `query_metadata`?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1554729099,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4MDgyNTM4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3055#issuecomment-480825384"},"message":"It could, but current `metadata()` does something that is not easily verbalizable, and I have no idea which aspects have any real purpose. IMHO, `metadata()` can simply be dropped, or used to implement whatever more complex or automagic behavior is desirable.","files":null}]}